  <h3>Import Maps</h3>=0A<p><code>&lt;script type=3D&quot;importmap&quot;&g=
t;</code></p>=0A<p><a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/bZQbuthkmDN=
e6VHk97ayRQ~~/AABEfhA~/Gdtt6T9Zp62_0NOApxMiVC265zbagE4790ngAJm-_hc8KsHotkkb=
uaG-8U8H_247xgFyp_XziOYauYby68gId4C1-GpqYTAzCN_GpNKjhbfCq6_L-moTs8ukqSLtaGX=
j6C3dR04l1imF3KAWoxLFy7usCY98OHYckv6biRvVooLfxWXZWn6C0-nPoeNr3-J_43_wUe0Kc0=
tc8Qn2oTFnYA~~">Import Maps</a> are pretty great! You get to write <code>im=
port thing from &quot;place&quot;;</code> and then you get to map what you =
mean by <code>&quot;place&quot;</code>. You could map it to a file in your =
project somewhere, that way you=E2=80=99ve got <em>one place</em> to update=
 it and update it everywhere that imports it. Or you could map it to somewh=
ere in a <em>node_modules</em> folder, meaning you don=E2=80=99t need a bun=
dler to do that job for you. Or you could map it to a fully qualified URL o=
ut there on the world wide internet, like a CDN that specializes in ESM stu=
ff.</p>=0A<p><a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/tvGt7U22DlEmmChFN=
w22iQ~~/AABEfhA~/w-bl1hmIqwF3y1XAMQtU8n33aUr2KzEZLKsdS9XTxyE2Uo4N40DG4nlBfg=
R4p8AZRme4jzPA8fNdppp21z9ucrwUVQjL8IxnWrHfTCY5GXjlFjeni8gW78TGg2Q13C32">The=
 CodePen Compiler</a> helps with that last one. <a href=3D"https://go.spark=
postmail2.com/f/a/BgJotLgrU4ZsqzcvycPFHA~~/AABEfhA~/JrYN-Epw0Nknrm8LkZE5g1N=
MRJk2lYhPqc05D3Y6ZMK-Du6Z7Q49-c2g8SPDWgfGBA9D-D6KV99IAApZ1Yyaj2KSOVP0UfEtyW=
q89GfcF89LclxRJIc01v-8WvHTp2lN3R-6CX64Ewz7SShbGNlbyg~~">We=E2=80=99ve got d=
ocs on it</a>.</p>=0A<p>Essentially you just write imports like you normall=
y would when you=E2=80=99re working on a project that uses npm and a bundle=
r to handle that sort of thing. The prototypical <code>import React from &q=
uot;react&quot;;</code> situation. Then CodePen Compiler makes sure an impo=
rtmap is in place to make it all work.</p>=0A<p>This way of doing things is=
 in the footsteps of Vite (or Skypack before it). In development, those too=
ls don=E2=80=99t bother bundling npm dependencies, they just rely on ESM an=
d link the resources where they are on disk. Then when individual files cha=
nge=E2=80=A6 that=E2=80=99s all that happens. Updates are fast and easy, be=
cause no big expensive re-bundling process needs to happen.</p>=0A<p>If you=
 were writing and maintaining import maps by hand, it would be cumbersome. =
For one thing, it has to be an inline chuck of code in a script tag in the =
head. So that inline chunk of code is repeated on every single HTML file of=
 your project, or at least the ones that need those JavaScript imports. It =
sure would be nice if the web supported linking out to a file instead. Lea =
Verou thinks so, and even discovered a nice little trick for making <a href=
=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/5nYTO6VA_YN8y5ywTUj6xQ~~/AABEfhA~/avA=
UhFVPFpSr0kn8yZVSgSnGlQDMCysT4dz_1h5g-q2zVGWc_fo6kkuxdi1D15PLVC_4Y0mArTb3Hl=
bDayJb4BEYJolNrlekBAQO6Wcz0yKl_rJE3aTtbDf3QvNvab-sUdvfH2FPka3jN5ORPZx9VWGzQ=
clyDXQKHBDXd_PjyfM~">External import maps, today!</a> Turns out the build-t=
ool-ish thing <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/gSmUrKq6HgLuTPqn=
SHKEBw~~/AABEfhA~/iOq6GCGDXdqrMPZib8e--yabVVU90z4UuAy0vbEs-qTtVffANy4IYwWSS=
77u-VldIU9V6pXo_SEJRkuWqtxCkw8UHdhaGkd84p6WcCVUZMBezPAQ5AcDBo4BaGuK202zAnWL=
XCH8bubNAyEQE3BoC-KG-Pb16iHWziktWGfm6lk~">JSPM does it the same way</a>. We=
 don=E2=80=99t really need to do this at CodePen as our compiler needs to i=
nline the importmap script anyway, it might as well contain the actual impo=
rtmap instead of just link to it.</p>=0A<p>It=E2=80=99s nice to see <a href=
=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/jez5lYx5JPA11sD2byZ9Xw~~/AABEfhA~/vkb=
ymPugX9ECGMESgO_8bxv-iN68e8bAo7u_miEu_Lzo2JVXsqpr-JR4ZQywyFaR5OLSztPKRrQt-6=
oOqTSHMhj-KJ6MkaaL0LdU80_t64QI9eaht2TmgyEaB15Po3XBfUF4NqUf85e_E6MZ11e5o9C1E=
y5Clkb7PuyEW2Er4di5jUAI-uUuCZOMB24Abd_b">Shopify weighing in on import maps=
</a> and trying to help make them more palettable for more widespread adopt=
ion. The fact that you can only have <em>one</em> of them is changing, whic=
h is nice. CodePen deals with that be coming any user-authored import maps =
it finds with the generated one, preferring the user choices.</p>=0A<p><a h=
ref=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/w9xHhEEVC61WPaoguT1ofg~~/AABEfhA~/=
Z4m32vqm2wSiK_xKvUAUet4CO78KqlOiOWcRnn3bHUkvcTnDBnOX_22WaB5p9Udksqcz8qKWpa6=
ZBqzDcPf3i7vbVmNl76cXLSeCUl_wF9r3ExE_qvhaT2UXJAJ1TNjS-xMRDZaxRyusPe5OZSptyA=
~~">Here=E2=80=99s a 52 second video</a> of using React on CodePen, which u=
ltimately works because of our import map implementation. And for the extra=
 curious, <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/YDkXcm0WsJONyd0O8G9j=
Fg~~/AABEfhA~/1z1qi_jm7e-wiyaie2RFuCaI6fOzUcV8DecDtTOTHUaz-56Mwr9p2kPY4-0ix=
IKXNPxA4vEbUXqpUI5dHGnvLP4MUbFBbWS_uy6gZkE_cqq5J08xe7RhqO6ueaL_6VesdrUO_xMw=
ZGzFCWpDG-hYTKuiS-u35ove2r_UYpFiZl4~">here=E2=80=99s a 29 minute podcast</a=
> of Alex and me talking about how it all came to be</p>=0D=0A             =
